 "notes": [
  "Cache arms (4b-prefix-cache, 9b-prefix-cache, 14b-ship) report TTFT from the COLD protocol only: the plateau protocol repeats prompts the cold one already cached, so their plateau ttft_ms_visit_means is {n: 0} by design.",
  "output_identity.n_distinct > 1 for a cell means that arm produced different bytes across visits for the same prompt; the shipped 14B does so on 2 of its plateau multi-turn cells (speed rows), so 'identical outputs' holds for the three arms of each of 4B and 9B, not for the 14B on long multi-turn prompts.",
  "Input-token counts in the cell labels are each arm's own tokenizer's (sizes in this data: 4B and 9B); the 14B tokenizer counts 811 (pa) and 6075 (ao-long).",
  "Plateau-protocol ratios are recorded but not used for conclusions: a faster arm heats less (see PERFORMANCE_LOG 2026-10-04)."
 ],
